---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const lastUpdated = 'September 2026';
---
<Layout
  path="/privacy-policy"
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Mithahara's privacy policy: what information we collect, how it's used, and how to contact us about it."
>
  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p class="page-meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <h3>What we collect</h3>
      <p>
        When you reach out by email or WhatsApp about Ahar orders, bulk enquiries, or one of our
        apps, we receive whatever contact details and order information you choose to share with
        us.
      </p>
      <p>
        For visitors who are only browsing, we use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count page views.
        It sets no cookies and stores nothing on your device. It records the page you landed on,
        the referring site, and coarse technical details such as country and browser — never a
        profile, and never anything that follows you to another site. We cannot identify you from
        it, and there is nothing to opt out of because nothing about you is retained.
      </p>

      <h3>How we use it</h3>
      <p>
        We use the information you send us only to respond to your enquiry, fulfil an order, or
        provide support for one of our apps. We don't sell or share your contact details with
        third parties.
      </p>

      <h3>Third-party apps</h3>
      <p>
        The Odoo apps and ClipMark are distributed through Odoo's app store and the Chrome Web
        Store respectively; each has its own listing and, where applicable, its own privacy
        disclosures at that store.
      </p>

      <h3>YouTube API Services</h3>
      <p>
        We publish our own app demo videos to our YouTube channel,{' '}
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@MithaharaApps">Mithahara Apps</a>, with an internal tool
        called Mithahara Uploader. It uses the YouTube API Services, and it is used only by
        Mithahara, on Mithahara's own channel. It is not offered to anyone else, and it never
        accesses another person's YouTube account or data.
      </p>
      <p>
        Through the API it uploads our videos and reads and updates their titles, descriptions,
        tags and privacy status. It keeps two things: the authorization token Google issues for our
        channel, stored only on our own machine and never shared, and the IDs of the videos we
        upload, which link each app's page to its video. It collects nothing about viewers, and
        shares nothing with third parties. It sets no cookies.
      </p>
      <p>
        By using YouTube you are subject to the{' '}
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms">YouTube Terms of Service</a>, and Google's
        handling of data is described in the{' '}
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a>. Access granted to
        the tool can be revoked at any time from the{' '}
        <a href="https://security.google.com/settings/security/permissions">Google security settings
        page</a>. When access is revoked, we delete the stored token straight away, and any other
        data obtained through the API within 30 days.
      </p>

      <h3>Contact</h3>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be sent to{' '}
        <a href="mailto:founder@mithahara.com">founder@mithahara.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
